# Share Links (Permanent)

## Law

**Tokenized access ≠ Web Publish slug profile.**

| Concern | Mechanism |
| --- | --- |
| Public SEO profile | `web_slug` / `web_published` — ADR 026 |
| **Share link** | `document_share_links` — opaque token, optional password, expiry, scope |

Do not overload web-publish slug routes for password/expiry links.

## Data model

Table `document_share_links` (always `business_id` + `document_id`):

- `token_hash` (unique) + `token_hint` — raw token returned **once** on create
- `password_hash` optional
- `scope` — `web` (HTML) \| `pdf` (download)
- `expires_at` nullable; `revoked_at` nullable (soft revoke)

Hash tokens/passwords with pepper (`SHARE_LINK_PEPPER`); never store raw secrets.

## Gates

- Create / list / revoke: writable + `@RequirePermission(documents.publish)`
- Create only when document status ∈ `{approved, published}`
- Public resolve: no JWT; check revoked / expiry / password
- Password attempts: Redis rate-limit (brute-force)

## Public routes

- `GET /api/public/share/:token` — meta (+ content if unlocked / no password)
- `POST /api/public/share/:token/unlock` — password gate → session + payload
- `GET /api/public/share/:token/file` — PDF bytes when `scope=pdf`

Web UI: `/[locale]/s/[token]`

## Render

Same source of truth as export: `ExportService.buildDocumentHtml` / PDF renderer — never a second layout engine.
